ed Kala Pani, Symbol of India\'s freedom struggle, Associated with sacrifices of freedom fighters like Veer Savarkar','Port Blair','Oct-Mar','4,500 to 7,000'),(9.030,'Dark Tourism','Uttarakhand','Trek to Roopkund Lake, Adventure activities & camping, Witness the mysterious human skeletons visible at the lake, Explore nearby Bedni Bugyal & Ali Bugyal, Enjoy Himalayan views of Trishul & Nanda Ghunti peaks','\"Skeleton Lake\" - remains of hundreds of humans dating back centuries, Mysterious historical & scientific significance, Famous high-altitude trekking destination','Roopkund','May-Jun','8,000 to 12,000'),(9.040,'Dark Tourism','Madhya Pradesh','Visit the abandoned Union Carbide plant site, Explore the Bhopal Gas Tragedy Memorials, Pay respects at the Remember Bhopal Museum, Learn about India\'s largest industrial disaster through heritage walks & museums','Site of the 1984 Bhopal Gas Tragedy - one of the world\'s worst industrial disasters, Symbol of corporate negligence & environmental justice, Memorials to thousands of victims','Union Carbide Plant','Oct-Mar','5,000 to 8,300'),(9.050,'Dark Tourism','Jharkhand','Visit the memorial honoring villagers killed during Naxalite violence, Learn about the history of left-wing extremism in the region, Explore nearby Topchanchi Lake for contrast between tragedy and nature','Site of a tragic massacre during the peak of Naxalite-police conflicts, Symbol of rural suffering due to insurgency, A reminder of the cost of socio-political unrest in Jharkhand','Topchanchi','Nov-Feb','2,500 to 4,500'),(9.060,'Dark Tourism','Bihar','Visit historical crime and justice-related landmarks, Explore Bhagalpur Central Jail, Learn about the Bhagalpur Blindings incident, Walk through old city areas linked to historical trials and events','Associated with the Bhagalpur Blindings case of the 1980s, which drew international attention, Symbol of justice system failures, Studied in criminology and human rights discussions','Bhagalpur','Oct-Mar','2,500 to 4,500'),(9.070,'Dark Tourism','Jharkhand','Witness the burning underground coal fires, Explore abandoned settlements and mining areas, Learn about the displacement of locals due to mine fires, Visit nearby Dhanbad city (\"Coal Capital of India\")','One of the world\'s oldest and largest underground coal fires (burning for over a century), Symbol of industrial exploitation and human displacement, Associated with pollution, danger, and socio-economic struggles','Jharia','Nov-Feb','2,500 to 4,500'),(10.010,'Yoga & Wellness','Uttarakhand','Yoga & meditation retreats at Parmarth Niketan, Sivananda Ashram and Yoga Niketan, Ayurvedic treatments & wellness therapies, Attend Ganga Aarti at Triveni Ghat, Nature walks & Himalayan trekking in surrounding areas','Known as the \"Yoga Capital of the World\", Famous for spiritual retreats, yoga training, and wellness tourism, Blend of ancient Indian spiritual practices, riverfront serenity & adventure activities','Rishikesh','Feb-Jun, Sep-Nov','2,500 to 5,000'),(10.020,'Yoga & Wellness','Kerala','Join yoga retreats & meditation sessions at beachfront resorts, Experience Ayurvedic massages, therapies & Panchakarma treatments, Samudra & Hawa Beaches for relaxation, Attend wellness workshops & holistic programs','Famous for Ayurveda & wellness tourism, Blend of beach leisure & holistic health retreats, Scenic cliffside yoga spots overlooking Arabian Sea, Ideal for stress relief, rejuvenation & spiritual wellness','Kovalam','Sep-Nov','3,000 to 5,000'),(10.030,'Yoga & Wellness','Goa','Join beachfront yoga retreats & meditation sessions, Attend Ayurveda and holistic wellness therapies, Explore Arambol, Anjuna & Palolem beaches, Participate in detox programs, Nature walks, cycling & mindfulness activities in coastal villages','Known as a wellness and yoga destination by the beach, Famous for Ayurveda retreats, meditation, and holistic wellness programs, Combines beach leisure, yoga, and rejuvenation, Vibrant wellness culture with a relaxed coastal lifestyle','Goa','Nov-Feb','3,600 to 6,000'),(10.040,'Yoga & Wellness','Karnataka','Join yoga retreats & Ashtanga yoga classes (Mysore is the birthplace of Ashtanga yoga in India), Visit Ayushakti for Ayurveda treatments, Attend meditation workshops & holistic therapy sessions','Known as the \"Yoga Capital of Karnataka\", Hub for Ayurveda & holistic wellness, Blend of spirituality, culture & wellness tourism, Famous for meditation, yoga teacher training & rejuvenation retreats','Mysore','Sep-Mar','4,500 to 6,000'),(10.050,'Yoga & Wellness','Himachal Pradesh','Visit Dalai Lama Temple Complex & Tsuglagkhang Monastery, Trekking in Triund & Kareri Lake, Explore Bhagsu Waterfall & Bhagsunath Temple, Attend Tibetan cultural festivals & meditation retreats, Paragliding, camping & nature walks','Known as the \"Little Lhasa\" of India, Headquarters of Tibetan government-in-exile, Spiritual & adventure tourism hub, Scenic Himalayan foothills with rich Tibetan culture','Dharamshala','Mar-Jun, Sep-Nov','3,000 to 5,000'),(10.060,'Yoga & Wellness','Maharashtra','Join yoga retreats, meditation, and wellness workshops, Attend Ayurvedic therapies & Panchakarma treatments, Spiritual visits to Trimbakeshwar Temple & Panchavati, Take part in Ganga Aarti at Godavari River ghats & treks in Anjneri Hills & Coin Forests','Known as a spiritual and wellness destination, Famous for Trimbakeshwar Shiva Temple & Godavari River ghats, Blend of yoga, Ayurveda, and spiritual wellness, Vineyards & serene natural surroundings ideal for rejuvenation','Nashik','Oct-Mar','6,000 to 8,000'),(10.070,'Yoga & Wellness','Tamil Nadu','Attend yoga, meditation & wellness programs at Isha Yoga Center, Visit Adiyogi Shiva statue, Explore the temple gardens and surroundings for photography & spiritual walks, Attend festivals like Mahashivratri at the center','Famous for Isha Yoga Center, a global hub for yoga and meditation, Adiyogi Shiva statue, recognized by Guinness World Records, Blend of spirituality, architecture & scenic Western Ghats backdrop','Coimbatore','Nov-Feb','7,500 to 8,000'),(10.080,'Yoga & Wellness','Rajasthan','Join yoga and meditation retreats near Pushkar Lake, Attend wellness workshops & holistic therapy sessions, Participate in Ganga Aarti , Explore Brahma Temple & local temples for spiritual wellness, Relax in peaceful ashrams & resorts','Known as a spiritual & wellness destination, Combines sacred lake, temples & yoga retreats, Famous for meditation, mindfulness & rejuvenation programs, Host of Pushkar Camel Fair, adding cultural and spiritual vibrancy','Pushkar','Oct-Feb','3,000 to 6,000'),(10.090,'Yoga & Wellness','West Bengal','Join yoga and meditation retreats in serene hilltop resorts, Nature walks & mindfulness treks to Durpin Dara, Deolo Hill & Pine View Nurseries, Attend holistic wellness workshops & Ayurveda sessions, Explore Buddhist monasteries for spiritual wellness','Known as a peaceful hill station with Himalayan views, Ideal for mindfulness, yoga, and holistic wellness retreats, Combines nature, spirituality, and clean air for rejuvenation, Lesser crowded compared to Darjeeling & Gangtok','Kalimpong','Mar-Jun, Sep-Nov','5,000 to 8,000'),(10.100,'Yoga & Wellness','Odisha','Join yoga retreats & meditation sessions near Puri Beach, Attend wellness and spiritual programs at ashrams, Participate in Ganga Aarti & spiritual rituals at Jagannath Temple, Explore Ayurvedic massages & therapies at wellness centers','Famous as a spiritual and wellness destination, Combines beach leisure with yoga, meditation & Ayurveda, Close to Jagannath Temple, adding a spiritual dimension to wellness, Ideal for stress relief, rejuvenation & holistic health','Puri','Nov-Feb','5,000 to 6,000'),(10.110,'Yoga & Wellness','West Bengal','Join yoga retreats & meditation sessions in hillside resorts, Morning sunrise yoga at Tiger Hill, Nature walks & mindfulness treks to Batasia Loop, Peace Pagoda, and tea gardens, Attend Ayurvedic & holistic wellness therapies, Explore Buddhist monasteries','Known as a Himalayan hill station for wellness & mindfulness, Combines nature, spirituality, and yoga, Clean mountain air & scenic tea gardens ideal for rejuvenation, Less crowded wellness retreats compared to mainstream hill tourism','Darjeeling','Mar-Jun, Sep-Nov','7,500 to 12,000'),(11.010,'Culinary','Delhi','Sample iconic street foods: Paranthe Wali Gali, chaat, samosas, kebabs & chole bhatura, Explore old markets for spices, sweets & local ingredients, Take a guided food walk to learn culinary history, Visit historic eateries like Karim\'s & Harnarains','Famous as one of India\'s oldest & busiest food hubs, Known for street food & Mughlai cuisine, Blend of heritage & culinary culture, Iconic destination for food lovers & gastronomic tours','Chandni Chowk, Old Delhi','Oct-Mar','3,000 to 5,000'),(11.020,'Culinary','West Bengal','Sample iconic Bengali sweets: Rasgulla, Sandesh, Mishti Doi, Street food tasting: Kathi rolls, puchkas, jhal muri, fish fry, Visit famous eateries like Peter Cat, 6 Ballygunge Place, Bhojohori Manna, Try Bengali thalis and seafood delicacies','Known as the food capital of East India, Famous for Bengali sweets, street food & Mughlai cuisine, Blend of heritage, colonial influence & local flavors, Iconic for culinary diversity and sweet culture','Kolkata','Nov-Feb','4,000 to 5,000'),(11.030,'Culinary','Maharashtra','Sample street foods: vada pav, pav bhaji, bhel puri, pani puri, Visit famous eateries: Leopold Café, Bademiya, Explore Chor Bazaar, Take guided culinary tours across South Mumbai, Bandra & Juhu, Try seafood & Parsi cuisine at authentic local joints','Known as a culinary melting pot of India, Famous for street food, seafood & Parsi cuisine, Blend of local Maharashtrian, street, Parsi, and international flavors, Iconic destination for food enthusiasts & gastronomic experiences','Mumbai','Oct-Mar','6,000 to 7,000'),(11.040,'Culinary','Rajasthan','Sample Rajasthani street food: dal baati churma, pyaaz ki kachori, ghevar, mirchi bada, Visit Chokhi Dhani for Rajasthani thali & cultural dining experience, Explore Johari Bazaar & Bapu Bazaar, Try lajawab Rajasthani thalis','Known as the \"Pink City of Culinary Delights\", Famous for Rajasthani sweets, thalis & street food, Blend of heritage, royal cuisine, and local flavors, Iconic for traditional cooking & food culture','Jaipur','Oct-Feb','3,000 to 5,000'),(11.050,'Culinary','Kerala','Taste Kerala seafood, Malabar biryani, appam & stew, meen curry, Explore Fort Kochi & Jew Town for street food, Visit famous eateries: Dhe Puttu, Kashi Art Café, The Rice Boat, Try traditional Kerala snacks & sweets: banana chips, pazham pori, halwa','Known as Kerala\'s culinary hub, Famous for seafood, Malabar cuisine & spice-influenced dishes, Blend of traditional Kerala flavors, Portuguese & Dutch culinary influences, Iconic destination for food lovers & gastronomic tourism','Kochi','Sep-Mar','3,000 to 5,500'),(11.060,'Culinary','Goa','Taste Goan seafood, Vindaloo, Xacuti, Bebinca, Sannas, Chorizo Pav & Dodol, Explore waterfront eateries along Mandovi River, Visit famous restaurants: Mum?s Kitchen, Ritz Classi, Participate in food tours to know the Goan culinary heritage','Known as Goa\'s culinary hub, Famous for seafood, Portuguese-influenced dishes & local beverages, Blend of traditional Goan cuisine, street food & fine dining, Iconic destination for food lovers & gastronomic experiences','Panaji','Nov-Feb','6,000 to 10,000'),(11.070,'Culinary','Tamil Nadu','Taste South Indian delicacies: dosa, idli, vada, sambar, filter coffee, Try Marina Beach Street food: sundal, bajji, Visit famous eateries: Murugan Idli Shop, Saravana Bhavan. Explore George Town & T Nagar for traditional snacks & sweets','Known as the gateway to South Indian cuisine, Famous for dosas, idlis, filter coffee & Marina Beach snacks, Blend of traditional, street, and modern culinary culture, Iconic destination for food lovers & gastronomic experiences','Chennai','Nov-Feb','2,500 to 5,000'),(11.080,'Culinary','Punjab','Taste Amritsari Kulcha, Lassi, Chole Bhature, Makki di Roti & Sarson da Saag, Visit Hall Bazaar & old city markets. Explore Golden Temple Langar for free communal meals, Try sweets: Jalebi, Gulab Jamun, and Pinni','Known as the culinary capital of Punjab, Famous for street food, Punjabi thalis & Langar at Golden Temple, Blend of heritage, cultural food traditions, and hearty flavors, Iconic destination for food lovers & gastronomic tourism','Amritsar','Oct-Feb','2,500 to 5,500'),(11.090,'Culinary','Gujarat','Taste famous Gujarati thali, dhokla, khakhra, fafda, jalebi, and undhiyu, Explore Manek Chowk Visit heritage restaurants like Gordhan Thal, Agashiye, and Honest, Try local sweets & snacks from street vendors and bakeries','Known as the culinary hub of Gujarat, Famous for Gujarati thalis, sweets & street food, Blend of traditional vegetarian cuisine and vibrant street food culture, Iconic destination for food lovers and gastronomic exploration','Ahmedabad','Oct-Feb','3,000 to 5,500'),(11.100,'Culinary','Telangana','Taste Hyderabadi Biryani, Haleem and Pathar ka Gosht, Explore Charminar & Laad Bazaar for street food like Osmania Biscuits and Irani Chai, Visit famous eateries: Bawarchi, Shah Ghouse, Try Qubani ka Meetha, Double Ka Meetha','Known as the \"City of Biryani & Nizami Cuisine\", Famous for rich Mughlai and Hyderabadi cuisine, Blend of street food, royal flavors, and culinary heritage, Iconic destination for food lovers and gastronomic experiences','Hyderabad','Oct-Feb','3,000 to 5,000'),(11.110,'Culinary','Chhattisgarh','Taste local tribal delicacies like Chousela, Angakar Roti, Bafauri, Dubki Kadhi, Dehrori and Tilgur, Experience traditional food festivals and village feasts, Visit weekly tribal markets for authentic snacks & drinks like Handia','Rice-based staple diet, Simple, healthy and eco-friendly tribal cuisine, Use of forest produce and natural ingredients, Unique fermented drinks and desserts','Raipur','Oct-Feb','2,500 to 3,500');
